circumventable-condition   linter  eligible               admission to censor, consul, tribunus rests on adrogatio, an act of censor that no office in effect can stop: eligible <-r_elig- holds_right <-r_rights- status <-r_adopt- adrogatio
closed-eligibility         linter  censor                 an act of the office reopens admission to it: censor -> (adrogatio) censor
dead-conclusion            linter  valid                  valid is concluded by r_act_ok and consumed by no rule
empty-right                linter  ius_commercii          right ius_commercii enters no condition
empty-right                linter  ius_conubii            right ius_conubii enters no condition
empty-right                linter  ius_suffragii          right ius_suffragii enters no condition
review-dead-end            linter  censor                 no office in effect can stop censor (adrogatio, establish_fact)
review-dead-end            linter  consul                 no office in effect can stop consul (execute)
review-dead-end            linter  tribunus               no office in effect can stop tribunus (intercessio) [clodius]
unchecked-act              linter  adrogatio by censor    adrogatio changes what status or admission rests on, no kind of action stops it, and nothing in effect restrains censor

power graph, period 13
office censor     [vacant]         may adrogatio, establish_fact
office consul     [vacant]         may execute
office tribunus   [clodius]        may intercessio
